course: dictionary
lesson: 14914
title: Finding something again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rediscovery is a noun. It means finding something again that had been lost, forgotten or hidden. Look at the word in parts: re means again, and discovery means finding something new. So a rediscovery is finding something you had lost or forgotten. «The rediscovery of the lost city thrilled the scientists.» The clue is lost: the city had gone missing, and now it was found again.
explain: The word can also mean enjoying or noticing something again after a long time. «After years in the attic, Priya made a rediscovery: her old sketchbook.» She had not drawn for ages, and finding the book brought back her love of drawing. This is a rediscovery of a hobby, not of a place.
explain: Look for the phrases «the rediscovery of» and «a rediscovery of». They tell you what was found again. «The rediscovery of an animal thought to be extinct made the news.» Extinct means no longer alive anywhere, so people thought it had gone for ever, and then it was seen again.
fact: Rediscovery is a noun, so you can say a rediscovery or rediscoveries.
fact: The word begins with re-, which means again.
fact: «Rediscovery» means finding something again that had been lost, forgotten or hidden.
fact: «Rediscovery» can also mean enjoying or noticing something again after a long time, such as a hobby or a writer.
fact: In history and science, a rediscovery can be a lost city, an old idea, or an animal thought to be extinct.
exercise: «The rediscovery of the lost city thrilled the scientists.» What does rediscovery mean here? | Closing a city for ever | Moving to the city by train | *Finding again a city that had been lost | Building a brand new city
exercise: «After years in the attic, Priya made a rediscovery: her old sketchbook.» What was rediscovered? | Her school bag | A new box of paints | The attic stairs | *Her love of drawing, a hobby she had let go
exercise: What does the prefix re- mean in rediscovery? | Not | Under | *Again | Before
test: Tom says a rediscovery is always about buying something new. What does rediscovery really mean? | Breaking something by accident | Buying something new | Something that has never been seen before | *Finding or enjoying something again
test: «Her rediscovery of the piano filled the quiet house with music.» What did she rediscover? | A piano teacher | A new piano | *Playing the piano again, a hobby she had once loved | A lost book
exam: Which is the best meaning of rediscovery in «the rediscovery of a lost temple»? | Painting a temple in bright colours | *Finding again something that had been lost | Building something new | Sleeping late in the morning
